 ## Background
-Pose Recentering is a standard preprocessing step in NeRF pipelines, particularly for datasets like LLFF (Local Light Field Fusion) where camera poses are not initially centered at the origin [S1, S3, unofficial]. The method was popularized by the original NeRF implementation [S1, unofficial] and is widely adopted in subsequent frameworks like NerfPl [S2, unofficial] and VoLoDSplat [S3, unofficial]. It addresses the issue of unbounded or poorly centered scenes, which can cause numerical issues in volume rendering and optimization.
